{title: Rise Again-E (tuned to Eb)}

Intro riff

4 bars of lead hits



{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]The night was cold, the sky was black
I walked that road alone
The wind was howlin’ at my back
But I kept pressin’ on
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]My faith was frayed, my hands were worn
[G]The ground was rough and steep
[A]The weight I carried felt like stone
[C]But steady I will [D]keep
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I rise[E] again, I won’t st[G]ay down
These [A]blues won’t be my [C]chain[D]s
I hear the [E]call, that steady [G]sound
Of [D]hope that still [A]remains

Big Riff!!!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I’ve lost some friends, I’ve paid the dues
And learned what I could take
But I’ve still got too much to lose
To let my spirit break
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus}
I rise[E] again, I won’t st[G]ay down
These [A]blues won’t be my [C]chain[D]s
I hear the [E]call, that steady [G]sound
Of [D]hope that still [A]remains

Quick Riff That Sam Hates

Interlude riff
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
You can knock me to the floor
But I won’t stay for long
Every crack just shows me more
Of what makes me strong
{end_of_bridge}


{start_of_bridge: Final Chorus}
I rise again, with every scar
They shine like morning rain
I’ve come too far, I know I am
The soul that won’t be tamed
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_bridge: Outro}
Yeah, I rise again —
No matter how it ends.
{end_of_bridge}